<title>FRANCE: EU grants free-mkt wheat, barley, oats, maize.</title>
<headline>EU grants free-mkt wheat, barley, oats, maize.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union on Thursday granted the following licences to export free-market grain to non-EU countries, member-country officials said</p>
<p>			 Tonnage		Maximum rebate</p>
<p> Soft wheat	  211,350		18.99 Ecus/tonne</p>
<p> Barley		 26,000		29.79 Ecus/tonne</p>
<p> Durum wheat	  12,000		 5.95 Ecus/tonne</p>
<p> Rye		    Rejected</p>
<p> Greek maize	  35,000		38.75 Ecus/tonne</p>
<p> Oats		    2,000		33.50 Ecus/tonne</p>
<p>(Finland/Sweden) to Switzerland-Liechtenstein</p>
</text>
